The GitLab commit-status + MR-note integration (`web/gitlab/`, shipped in `5e88d77`) had **no env-var wiring in `application.yml`** — unlike the GitHub block — so a deployment had no documented on-switch. This adds the mirrored `${UNITRACK_GITLAB_*}` block, defaulting **disabled**:

```yaml
gitlab:
  enabled: ${UNITRACK_GITLAB_ENABLED:false}
  token:   ${UNITRACK_GITLAB_TOKEN:}
  api-url: ${UNITRACK_GITLAB_API_URL:https://gitlab.com/api/v4}   # override for self-hosted
  server-base-url: ${UNITRACK_BASE_URL:http://localhost:8080}
  context: ${UNITRACK_GITLAB_CONTEXT:unitrack/quality-gate}
  mr-note: ${UNITRACK_GITLAB_MR_NOTE:true}
```

Relaxed binding already mapped these env vars; this makes the switch discoverable and the API URL overridable for self-hosted GitLab. Posting logic is unchanged and already covered by `GitLabServiceTest`.

**Live dogfood is still pending** — the shared GitLab.com token is currently expired (tracked separately); once refreshed, enable on the lab against `gitlab-smoketest` and confirm a commit status posts.

